 ## 2026-09-22
 
+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev9 — census integrity, in-flight probe bounds, validated replay, attribution repair
+
+- P1 FIXED (receipt-namespace directory fails closed): the peer census skipped every directory before reading, so a directory at the exact `<client-UUID>.json` receipt path read as no peers and admitted a second client without `multi_attach`. The census now skips only staging (`attach-*`) and non-receipt names; any other entry — including a directory — must read as a valid receipt file or the attach refuses. Narrowings `N-attach-peers-dir` (termbind) and `N-attach-peers-dir-skip` (tmuxserver, cross-package plant) KILLED through the census test and the entry test; new census row peershape.
+- P2-A FIXED (read-only probes honor the deadline in-flight): the stop poll, the terminate-stale self-confirm, and the status live probes ran under the caller's context while the deadline lived only in a field/clock checks, so a blocked probe waited past the bound. One shared `probeContext` (duration-derived, fake-clock-safe: answered probes follow the clock exactly, only never-answered probes conclude by the context) now bounds all three; expiry concludes unknown, never a verdict. Release-controlled entry tests pin refusal-before-release with no kill/closure/termination/report. Shared narrowing `N-probe-deadline` KILLED through all three entries with isolated single-test attribution. Runner audit: every other wait/probe is deadline-bounded (barrier/admission/boundary/dial); single-shot commits stay caller-cancellation-bounded as stated bound B45 (engine-mirrored; a hung commit hangs, never mis-verdicts).
+- P2-B NARROWED (receipt-validated replay with a peer present): the overlap gate demanded overlap capabilities before consulting the durable store, so an identical same-client retry with another peer present refused `capability_unproven`. A Lookup-proven recorded receipt now exempts the retry (replay, or `idempotency_mismatch` when transport/input changed, after the live authorization recheck); a client with no recorded receipt still gates however it names itself. Pin: input + read-only replay shapes with an input peer, plus the conflicting-retry mismatch leg. Narrowing `N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven` KILLED; census row overlapreplay; B44 clarified (validated replay here, liveness with TASK-260922-vcx6yo).
+- P2-D REPAIRED (isolated kill attribution): the three shared escalation/wait plants claimed per-entry kills the fixtures could not deliver (quiesce auth subtest at exact expiry under the -1h plant; strictly-past deadline case vs the equal-instant narrowing; boundary-commit 7h advance vs the +1h widening). Fixtures now drive the admitted class (30-min-past expiry, on-deadline instant leg, 6.5h advance with release-controlled barrier) and every shared plant kills through every claimed killer ALONE, twice, with the companion/precision legs green — stop 4 / quiesce 4 and 4 wait killers measured, not claimed. Census: 148 gates, 266 measured of 5504 (pollbound measured; terminate tail corrected U1→B39); battery 296/296 + 42/42.
+- P2-C REPAIRED (evidence freshness): the rev9 evidence archive is built from the frozen rev9 tree and attached with its absolute path, then read back and digest-verified from the board — the stale-archive failure is closed by construction, not by prose.
+
+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev8 — post-wait revalidation, bounded waits, overlap fail-closed
+
+- P1-A FIXED (stop escalation + quiesce mid-sequence): the stop escalation revalidates the operation deadline, AX authorization over the live lease, and server generation after its poll before `kill-session` issues — a graceful timeout escalates, any other stale fact refuses without the kill — and the quiesce detach revalidates between the lock and detach commands. The two post-wait boundaries share one closure over the landed gates (same `CheckAuthorization` call, same generation read, row's own timeout code) with per-site skip narrowings; sibling paths probed with fact-mutation during their waits: create/restore single-command (rotation changes nothing), terminate tail (kill count stays one, refusal stands), boundary tail (post-signal command is the read-only rows probe). Graceful wait and operation deadline are distinct bounds. Narrowings: 3 shared arms + 2 per-site skips, all KILLED with per-test attribution; census effectrecheck stop 4 / quiesce 4.
+- P2 FIXED (bounded waits, uniform barrier contract): the attach admission and barrier acquisition run under one wait context combining the operation deadline with caller cancellation — the entry bounds the wait itself (goroutine + select, late answers discarded), so even a non-cooperative adapter cannot hold the request past its deadline or commit late. Quiesce span and boundary report commit acquire through the same contract (row's own timeout code; boundary reports against its committed proof). Release-controlled tests prove refusal-before-release plus no-late-receipt; cancellation returns promptly. Narrowing `N-attach-wait-deadline` KILLED through all four deadline tests while the cancellation companion stays green.
+- P1-B NARROWED (overlap fail-closed): this leaf has no liveness census, so a stored peer receipt reads as possibly live — a second client needs `multi_attach`, new input over an input peer needs `multiple_input_clients`, same-client retries exempt, unreadable peers fail closed. Over-strict by design (detached clients' receipts still trigger) until the liveness census lands; owner TASK-260922-vcx6yo, stated as B44. Narrowings `N-attach-overlap-multi` / `-input` KILLED with two-peer precision legs. The §4.C attach row claims only the fail-closed gate, never liveness.
+- PROCESS: a new downstream bound shadows an upstream narrowing when it refuses the same member with the same verdict — the entry-deadline instant row is reclassified as survived-supplementary `D-attach-entry-deadline-shadowed` (enforced boundary measured at post-lock + wait), with deterministic fired-context pre-checks so the shadowing never races. An ordering-lock plant must skip the acquisition, not acquire-then-release (the wait alone preserves the order and the row survives). Census: 261 measured of 5376 (new rows effectrecheck/overlapmulti/overlapinput/waitbound), battery 293/293 + 41/41.
