+## 2026-09-22
+
+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rev7 — attach effect-boundary enumeration; authkind evidence repair
+
+- P1+P2-A FIXED (same invariant, one enumeration): the attach admission-to-effect interval that rev6 closed for closure stayed open for generation and the request deadline. The post-lock boundary now revalidates every live fact — closure (existing recheck), server generation (new live `CurrentGeneration` read), request deadline (new live clock read, lock wait counted, kept distinct from authorization expiry) — while authorization expiry, transport, and input binding revalidate inside the commit call itself (`AttachStore.Attach` rechecks with the live clock and holds no wait before the no-replace install); transition, operation capability, and backend identity are pure checks over request-immutable members with nothing to revalidate. SPEC §4.C 1095 ("rechecked immediately before each side effect") is the pin. Regressions: rotation-during-lock-wait (channel-ordered, deterministic), admission-advances-clock-past-deadline with valid authorization, and the on-the-instant variant. Narrowings `N-attach-postlock-generation` / `N-attach-postlock-deadline` KILLED; sibling members (late instants) still refuse under the plants. Create/restore/stop never had the interval: the landed engine `runEffects` and this leaf's `runLifecycleEffects` recheck deadline+authorization+generation before every effect including the first, after any wait. Residual (B42 extended): a rotation between the recheck and the commit, in- or cross-process, in a wait-free window.
+- P2-B CLOSED: `TestAttachAuthorizationMembersRefuseWithoutReceipt` (expiry/input/transport) asserts refusal AND receipt absence through `Execute(attach)`; `N-attach-input-escalation` (reviewer A3 shape on the landed gate, cross-package row) commits the receipt before the result binding refuses, so the killer's absence assertion reddens. Gate stays landed, no fork.
+- P3 CLOSED: the two effect-loop authkind wirings are reclassified as supplementary `D-` rows (they refuse a permitted grant; they admit nothing), the entry authkind rows are converted to genuine no-bind narrowings (control-kind bodies bind under the plant and refuse only at the loop), and the shared loop side is measured by the genuinely admitting `N-lifecycle-loop-authorization` (pre-commit auth failures execute the first effect; post-commit still refuse), killing through both terminate and restore entries with per-entry attribution. Census: 256 measured of 5248 (generation EXA U1→M), symmetry lines recounted, battery 285/285 (279 N + 5 D + control).
+- PROCESS: a new post-lock arm textually identical to the entry arm breaks the entry row's anchor count AND silently converts its kill into a reroute (the post-lock arm refuses the same verdict); the entry killer now asserts the admission never ran, pinning the refusal to the entry site. A shared-loop narrowing needs a killer per entry or one side is attribution-by-assertion.
